==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Manga Moemoe Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Despite being a titan clone, it has identical stats to its original counterpart which makes it stronger than most variants that were designed to specialize against certain traits. She has high health, high attack power, and can manage well in stages where [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]] would also be effective. It's important that peons are cleared for her so that she can reach her destined target, such as bosses, due to the lack of good range. She does fall off naturally where level 30 Titan Cat stops being viable, but since Unite! is in a mid-[[Legend Stages/SoL|SOL]] meta, Manga Daragogogo Cat would still be usable to what is still considered early-mid game in the mobile version.

{{Job|Classification = Tanker & Melee}}

